AN   oxalosuccinate carboxylase.
CA   D-threo-isocitrate + NADP(+) = 2-oxoglutarate + CO2 + NADPH.
CC   -!- Unlike EC 1.1.1.41, oxalosuccinate can be used as a substrate.
CC   -!- In eukaryotes, isocitrate dehydrogenase exists in two forms: an
CC       NAD(+)-linked enzyme found only in mitochondria and displaying
CC       allosteric properties, and a non-allosteric, NADP(+)-linked enzyme
CC       that is found in both mitochondria and cytoplasm.
CC   -!- The enzyme from some species can also use NAD(+) but much more
CC       slowly.
